<%# The collection grid: one page of the grid's cards in order, one per
    game, in columns filling the row, each drawn as its grid face (sized by
    its slot). An owned game shows the edition it shows, its copies across
    editions ("x3", from x1, in an accent box at the top-right), under them
    the editions held when two or more ("2 éd.", in the same box) and, when
    an edition was gained since the player last saw their collection,
    "Nouveau" in a lime box at the top-left. With `set_apart`, a game the
    player does not hold shows its face faded, grey and locked, its link
    named "not owned" after the card's title, rarity and season; without, it
    shows its plain face, named as an owned one. Each leads to its card's
    detail, carrying the grid's filters and search, so the detail walks this
    grid as shown (◀ ▶) and leads back to it. No card: the empty-filter
    line, or,
    past the last page of a grid that has cards, the past-the-end line.
    - context: the grid's filters and search, as a detail's `grid`
      parameter carries them (CollectionGridLoading#grid_context);
    - slots: [ [ Catalog::CardView, Game::HeldGames::Edition | nil ], … ];
    - set_apart: true for a signed-in player, whose cards not held are set
      apart from theirs;
    - pagy: the grid's page;
    - new_badge: whether an edition gained since the viewer last saw their
      collection is marked (the viewer's own grid only). %>
<% if slots.empty? %>
  <p class="collection-grid__empty"><%= pagy.count.positive? ? t("library.grid.past_the_end") : t("library.grid.empty") %></p>
<% else %>
  <ol id="collection-slots" class="collection-grid collection-grid--fill" aria-label="<%= t("library.grid.label") %>">
    <%= render "library/slots", slots:, context:, set_apart:, new_badge: %>
  </ol>
<% end %>
<%= render "library/pages", pagy:, empty: slots.empty? %>
